Feature: Everyone starts from cold
  In a game, every plane starts in the same way: on the ground and disarmed. Nobody can arm
  before GO. At GO, every pilot arms, takes off and flies away. The computer pilots do the
  same with their radios, so nobody has a head start.

  Expectation: A race starts with every plane on the ground
    The game panel counts down at once: there is nothing to wait for, because nobody is in the
    air yet.
    Overrides: G starts a race
    Given the game clock is off
    When the pilot starts a race
    Then the game is a race
    And the game clock is counting down
    And the vehicle is disarmed
    And the opponents are on the ground

  Expectation: Nobody arms before GO
    The arm switch does nothing until GO. A plane that is armed early has a head start.
    Overrides: The arm switch arms the vehicle
    Given the game clock is counting down
    And the vehicle is disarmed
    When the arm switch is on
    Then the vehicle is disarmed

  Expectation: At GO the arm switch arms your plane
    If the arm switch is on at GO, the autopilot arms the plane at once.
    Given the game clock is counting down
    And the arm switch is on
    When the countdown ends
    Then the game clock is running
    And the vehicle is armed

  Expectation: The computer pilots take off after GO
    At GO, each computer pilot puts its arm switch on. Then it takes off straight up in QHOVER,
    and it pushes the FBWA button to fly on the wing. That takes about as long as it takes you.
    Given the game clock is counting down
    And the opponents are on the ground
    When the countdown ends
    Then the opponents are flying
